		"description": {
			"public": "<p><strong>Weapon Kit</strong> &middot; <em>Engineer invention. Counts as a weapon for swapping and stowing. Toolbelt options cost 2 Actions and 1 Toolbelt scrap.</em></p><hr><p><strong>Flame Jet (basic) &mdash; 1 Action.</strong> Reach 4, 1d8 Fire. Double damage if the target is Smoldering. Ignores armor. On crit: apply Smoldering.</p><p><strong>Toolbelt (2 Actions, 1 scrap):</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Flame Blast.</strong> Cone 3, 2d8 Fire. On hit: inflict Smoldering. Ignores armor.</li><li><strong>Air Blast.</strong> Reach 4, 3d8 Fire. On a failed STR save, Large and smaller targets are pushed back INT spaces. Can't miss Smoldering targets, and Smoldering targets automatically fail.</li><li><strong>Napalm.</strong> Reach 4, Wall 4. Lasts 1 minute or until dispersed. Targets that start or end a turn adjacent to it, or enter an adjacent space, take KEY Fire damage. Ignores armor.</li></ul><p><strong>High Levels:</strong> +5 damage every 5 levels (Flame Jet, Flame Blast, Air Blast); +2 damage every 5 levels (Napalm).</p><hr><p><em>[A] Flame Jet rolls 1d8 Fire (+5 per 5 levels), ignoring armor, and applies Smoldering on a crit.</em></p><p><em>[A] Each Toolbelt option is its own \"Flamethrower: …\" feature granted with the kit; using one spends 1 Toolbelt scrap — tracked on the sheet (click the counter to correct mistakes).</em></p><p><em>[M] Double the damage if the target is Smoldering.</em></p>",
